  {
   "s": "CDSL",
   "n": "Central Depository Services (India) Limi",
   "cat": "Outcome of Board Meeting",
   "when": "2026-08-27 14:02",
   "sent": "neutral",
   "txt": "### 1. Single Most Important Fact\n* **Leadership Transition:** CDSL has appointed **Shri Farokh Patel** (previously Senior VP \u2013 Audit, Inspection & Compliance) as the **Chief Regulatory Officer & Compliance Officer** (Senior Management Personnel / Key Management Personnel) effective **September 1, 2026**, succeeding **Smt. Nayana Ovalekar**, who ceases to hold the position at the close of business on **August 31, 2026**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Key Numbers\n* *No financial figures, operating metrics, or contract values are disclosed in this filing.*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Management Guidance & Forward Statements\n* None provided.\n\n---\n\n### 4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On\n* **No action required:** This is a planned internal succession/statutory compliance transition in key regulatory management. \n\n---\n\n### 5. One-Line Net Read\n* **Neutral:** Routine internal appointment and regulatory leadership transition with no material impact on operations or financials."
  },
  {
   "s": "JIOFIN",
   "n": "Jio Financial Services Limited",
   "cat": "Change in Director(s)",
   "when": "2026-08-26 19:55",
   "sent": "positive",
   "txt": "**1. Single Most Important Fact**\nAt the 3rd Annual General Meeting (Post Listing) held on August 26, 2026, shareholders approved the **re-appointment of Shri Hitesh Kumar Sethia as Managing Director and CEO** for a 5-year term effective November 15, 2026, and the **appointment of PKF Sridhar & Santhanam LLP** as Joint Statutory Auditors for a 3-year term (until the 2029 AGM), replacing Lodha & Co LLP alongside Deloitte Haskins & Sells.\n\n**2. Key Numbers**\n* No financial metrics, revenues, margins, or contract values were disclosed in this corporate governance filing.\n\n**3. Management Guidance & Forward-Looking Statements**\n* None stated in the document.\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**\n* **Leadership Continuity:** Confirms long-term leadership stability under MD & CEO Hitesh Kumar Sethia for the next 5 years starting November 15, 2026.\n* **No action required** as the AGM voting/approval process is concluded.\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**\n* **Neutral to Mildly Positive:** Routine governance update providing leadership continuity and standard statutory auditor rotation without material operational or financial surprises."
  },
  {
   "s": "NTPC",
   "n": "NTPC Limited",
   "cat": "Action(s) taken or orders passed",
   "when": "2026-08-26 13:42",
   "sent": "neutral",
   "txt": "**1. Single Most Important Fact**\nBSE and NSE have issued notices imposing a fine of \u20b95,36,900 each (inclusive of GST) on NTPC for the quarter ended 30th June 2026 due to non-compliance with Regulation 17(1) of SEBI Listing Regulations (pertaining to Board composition / requisite number of Independent Directors).\n\n---\n\n**2. Key Numbers Exactly as Stated**\n* **Fine Amount:** \u20b95,36,900/- (inclusive of GST) each by BSE and NSE (Total: \u20b910,73,800/-).\n*(No other financial metrics/results are reported in this filing).*\n\n---\n\n**3. Management Guidance, Outlook, or Forward Statements**\n* NTPC has replied to the exchanges requesting them not to levy the fines, clarifying that as a Government Company, the power to appoint directors rests solely with the President of India through the Ministry of Power (MoP).\n* The company stated it is *\"consistently pursuing the matter with the MoP for appointment of the requisite number of Independent Directors on the Board\"* to restore compliance.\n\n---\n\n**4. What a Shareholder Should Watch or Act On**\n* Watch for government notifications regarding the appointment of Independent Directors to achieve full compliance with SEBI LODR board composition norms.\n* Watch for responses from BSE/NSE regarding NTPC's request to waive the levied fines.\n\n---\n\n**5. One-Line Net Read**\n* **Neutral**: The financial penalty is negligible for a company of NTPC's scale, and this non-compliance is a standard procedural/administrative delay typical of PSUs awaiting central government board appointments."
  }
